# Mechanism: from-agda-cubical — pinned agda/cubical library clone, registered
# in the Agda user libraries file. The cubical Agda proof lane (provided-view
# univalence obligation — docs/letters/from-soraya-univalence-lane-routing.md,
# workitem 081KX1VE4G808QG0R003DCK3GV).
# Realizer: src/Core.TypeScript/ace/setup-realizers/from-agda-cubical.ts
#   (delegates to tools/setup/common/agda-cubical.sh — single implementation).
#
# The Agda BINARY comes from the system package manifests (manifests/brew
# `agda`, manifests/apt `agda`) — bottled/binary installs, NOT the ghcup+cabal
# source build Soraya's spec offered as the heavy fallback (her §4 lighter-path
# clause taken: system packages exist on both OSes, so no 30-90 min GHC build).
#
# Format:
#   cubical  <git-repo-url>  <release-tag>  agda=<agda-version-prefix>  commit=<tag-commit-sha>
#
# PIN-PAIR DISCIPLINE (Soraya's spec, adapted): each row is a content-pin pair
# — a cubical release tag bound to the Agda version line it supports (from the
# upstream release notes, https://github.com/agda/cubical/releases: each release
# names its exact compatible Agda). agda-cubical.sh selects the row whose
# agda= prefix matches the INSTALLED `agda --version`, then asserts the cloned
# tag's HEAD equals commit= (supply-chain assert; fail loudly on mismatch).
#
# NAMED DEBT (soft pin): the Agda binary version is whatever brew/apt ship
# (brew 2026-07-08: 2.8.0; Ubuntu noble apt: 2.6.3; plucky/questing: 2.6.4.3;
# resolute+: 2.8.0). If a distro drifts to an Agda with no row below, the
# install WARNS and skips the lane (it does not fail the install) — the fix is
# to add/bump a row here from the matching upstream cubical release. Bump
# procedure: pick the cubical release whose notes name the new Agda version,
# update tag= + commit= together (commit is the tag's commit sha, via
# `git ls-remote https://github.com/agda/cubical.git refs/tags/<tag>`).

